\begin{align*}
AC: \quad y &= (2a)x - a^2, \\
BC: \quad y &= (2b)x - b^2.
\end{align*}
Since the lines $AC$ and $BC$ both pass through the point $(0,c),$ we can substitute $x = 0$ into the equations above to get:
